        "tsrs kind numbering is hard-coded in `NO_ASSIGNMENT_DECLARATION`. A test reads Cargo.lock and fails unless tsrs is exactly 0.24.0, so a version bump is caught in every nextest run.",
        "Chakra is the large-scale corpus for perf checks. Regression checks compare output to main across 10 corpus runs and use a compare-everything build to confirm zero disagreements.",
        "Work happens in worktrees under `.claude/worktrees/`. The #519 branch is `fix-519c`.",
        "Request counts live per-instance in the `Rpc::calls` map. Budget tests that read a process-wide counter can interfere with each other when run in parallel."
