          "path": "crates/semantic/src/rpc.rs",
          "line": 213,
          "finding": "`settled_readonly` settles false from check flags when no value declaration exists, so it depends on hard-coded tsrs 0.24 kind numbers. It should return early before parsing declaration handles when an earlier guard already means 'ask the checker'."
        },
        {
          "path": "crates/semantic/src/convert.rs",
          "line": 839,
          "finding": "The doc on `State::readonly` claims the answer is kept only for lists with an unsettled property, but `Converter::readonly` caches every list through `Answers::get`. The comment was corrected, and the memo is kept for every list."
        },
        {
          "path": "crates/semantic/src/convert.rs",
          "line": 1100,
          "finding": "In `Flights::board`, a walk that misses the memo can become Lead for a conversion whose leader just finished, and then redo the work without re-reading the memo. Output is correct but the work is wasted (#514 follow-up)."
        },
        {
          "path": "crates/semantic/src/lib.rs",
          "line": 358,
          "finding": "`EarlyStart::fits` no longer compares root files, so a session opened for other roots is adopted and rerooted. Reads made during the reroot may not be recorded, which could leave a stale kept answer (#515 follow-up needing a test)."
